170
00:14:31,660 --> 00:14:36,380
You know, I love to go backpacking. It's always been one of the favorite things I've,

171
00:14:37,060 --> 00:14:43,440
my favorite outdoor activities. My dad used to take us backpacking when we were kids,

172
00:14:43,440 --> 00:14:48,940
and we did a couple of family trips that way, and some I very fondly remembered.

173
00:14:49,600 --> 00:14:57,000
So several years ago, I decided that I wanted to cover a few more miles, and I had a free week,

174
00:14:57,140 --> 00:15:01,820
and I decided that I would go backpacking, and I had a buddy drive me out to the trailhead

175
00:15:01,820 --> 00:15:08,960
and took off for four or five days of solo backpacking, and I ended it early because

176
00:15:08,960 --> 00:15:13,200
I could not stand it. I really did not enjoy myself at all.

177
00:15:13,440 --> 00:15:18,880
It didn't take long to figure out why. It was because I did not get to go with the people

178
00:15:18,880 --> 00:15:24,740
that I liked to go backpacking with, my fellow leaders and the scouts from the scout troop.

179
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:29,560
So I learned a little something about myself and about the nature of some of the scouting

180
00:15:29,560 --> 00:15:34,820
activities that we do. I recently had somebody ask me, they were in a bit of a conundrum about

181
00:15:34,820 --> 00:15:48,020
which troop of several choices their son should join. He described one real kind of like super troop,

182
00:15:48,500 --> 00:15:56,300
one really kind of overachieving big giant troop that had lots and lots of amenities in their own scout hut,

183
00:15:56,300 --> 00:15:57,740
and et cetera, et cetera, et cetera, et cetera.

184
00:16:01,740 --> 00:16:10,740
And one of the other choices, I mean, understand this guy and his son had visited like seven different troops

185
00:16:10,740 --> 00:16:16,280
and a couple of them twice. I know, a little more energy than I have.

186
00:16:16,280 --> 00:16:24,579
But one of the other troops was kind of smaller and maybe not as high functioning and everything

187
00:16:24,579 --> 00:16:27,360
and had a bit less to recommend it.

188
00:16:27,540 --> 00:16:34,780
But the fellow's son had been trying to convince one of his buddies from his Weevilos den

189
00:16:34,780 --> 00:16:38,140
to go and join the big troop with him and wasn't getting anywhere.

190
00:16:38,140 --> 00:16:45,100
Most of the other boys in the troop were going to join the smaller troop,

191
00:16:45,819 --> 00:16:50,020
the one that looked less desirable on paper.

192
00:16:50,420 --> 00:16:55,400
So my advice to him was, well, you know, would your son be happy going backpacking on his own?

193
00:16:55,980 --> 00:17:00,080
Or would he rather be playing in the backyard with a bunch of his buddies?

194
00:17:00,760 --> 00:17:05,200
If he was able to go to Disneyland on his own, what kind of a time do you think he would have?

195
00:17:05,200 --> 00:17:12,260
Would he be able to go out and make friends and enjoy the experience, you know, with new friends on his own?

196
00:17:12,620 --> 00:17:18,620
Or would he kind of find it hollow because he wasn't enjoying it with the people that he knew and loved?

197
00:17:18,960 --> 00:17:20,880
You know, there's really not a right or a wrong answer.

198
00:17:21,040 --> 00:17:23,180
It's just a matter of personality.

199
00:17:24,440 --> 00:17:30,100
Did I, you know, that would be the way that I would arrive at that decision.

200
00:17:30,100 --> 00:17:37,500
And the other thing is, and it's important to remember this, scouts don't marry troops.

201
00:17:37,639 --> 00:17:39,399
They don't sign a contract with a troop.

202
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:43,219
It's not till death do us part.

203
00:17:43,500 --> 00:17:46,740
What it is, is it's more like buying a pair of shoes.

204
00:17:46,959 --> 00:17:50,959
Try on a few pairs sometimes before you find one that fits real well.

205
00:17:51,419 --> 00:17:52,600
And it's the same with a scout troop.

206
00:17:52,600 --> 00:18:01,179
I've had no qualms at all about boys changing from my scout troop to one that's a better fit for them.

207
00:18:01,639 --> 00:18:03,959
Well, anyway, how do you choose a scout troop?

208
00:18:04,500 --> 00:18:10,659
Is it based on the amenities of the troop and things like that?

209
00:18:11,340 --> 00:18:13,360
Yeah, I guess in part.

210
00:18:13,360 --> 00:18:23,240
But it's also got to do with the broader concepts of being able to move on in scouting.

211
00:18:23,639 --> 00:18:25,780
A lot of guys are going to need their buddies to do that.

